1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
TeamClu — the loop your team’s AI work actually runs on.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Most AI tooling starts at build and stops there. TeamClu is the claim that the loop closes.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:25,000
One session. Teammates and agents in the same context — @mention an agent and it answers as a participant.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:34,000
The agent runs on your machine. Only the assets are shared.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:49,000
An agent does not talk in bubbles. It answers in notes — and the diff reviewer is built the same way.

6
00:00:49,000 --> 00:01:04,000
The result becomes a team asset, not a dotfile. Publish once with a changelog and every teammate’s agent follows it.

7
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:13,000
The result is a team asset, not a dotfile — so the next round starts faster. That is the whole loop.

8
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:21,000
And it runs when you are not at the desk — same session, same capabilities, in WeCom, Feishu, Discord, KOOK, WeChat or Email.

9
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:27,000
TeamClu — MIT licensed, open source, in beta. teamclu.ai
